<global rules>
  Use comments sparingly. Inline comments should only be used when the code itself cannot express the reason behind a decision
  Always use Test Driven Development. First create comprehensive tests for the feature, then write the feature itself, ensuring all tests pass
  When a feature integrates systems, apply TDD with integration tests
  When a feature completes end-to-end usage of the application, apply TDD with E2E tests
  Implement error handling for possible runtime failures that tests cannot catch
  Adjustable data should be kept decoupled from the application code
  Docs should never quote adjustable data values.
  Docs that reflect current state of the application should never cite changes done, reasons for changes, fixes
  Decisions made and dead-ends encountered should be logged in ./docs/decision_log.md
  In cases where alternative architectures were considered, ADR should be made in ./docs elaborating on the decision
  Update CHANGELOG.MD after every feature development with a concise summary of what changed
  ARCHITECTURE.md must contain a concise architectural overview of the existing elements. More specific feature descriptions may be created in ./docs as appropriate
  USER-GUIDE.md must contain a concise, human-friendly instruction on how to use existing features
  ./docs/requirements.md contains the full project requirements
  Before starting work, follow ./docs/agent-workflow.md: ./docs/roadmap.md names the current stage and ./docs/specs/ holds its contract
  ADRs live in ./docs/adr/; evals/questions.yaml is the behavioural definition of the agent and must be kept in sync with behaviour changes
</global rules>
